// Motion Prompt #048 · MIT License (c) 2026 Shohei Ohtaki · https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#048
//
// L-cut / Lカット
// Pack: camera (Camera moves & transitions) · element 24 · Category: Transitions
// What happens: The previous scene's audio carries on for a while after the picture has changed; the picture is shown on top with video and audio timelines below.
// Motion spec:
//   - Join: the picture is a straight cut; only the audio switches to the next scene (B) after the picture does. The offset is 20% of the timeline (0.72 s)
//   - Playhead: moves left to right at constant speed over 3.6 s (0.4 s to 4.0 s); picture switches at 55% (about 2.38 s), audio at 75% (about 3.10 s)
//   - In the offset section (55–75%) the picture is already B while the audio is still A; the section is marked with a pale blue band and two blue dashed lines
//   - Layout: the top 134 px is the picture (fixed camera, subjects do not move); the bottom 74 px holds two timeline rows, video and audio (A grey, B pale blue, waveform on the audio row)
//   - Labels: "映像A / 映像B" (video A / B) at bottom left of the picture; the audio now playing at bottom right ("♪ Aの音" grey → "♪ Bの音" blue)
//   - Return: cross-fade back to the start over the last 0.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s)
// When to use it: To keep a speaker's voice running while showing the listener's reaction or related footage.
// Tags: l-cut, l cut, split edit, audio lag, sound carries over, audio transition, edit
// Size: 539x208 px · Cycle: 9.4 s
// Needs: kit camera -> https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/camera.js
// Live demo: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#048
//
// cells[i](k, w, h, u): k = CanvasRenderingContext2D (already cleared and wrapped in save/restore by the caller), w,h = size, u = seconds in [0, cycle). The picture depends only on u.
// Element code starts here. CELLS, constants and helpers live in the kit.

// @element 24
// 24 Lカット: 映像が先に次の場面（B）へ切り替わり、前の場面（A）の音が残る
CELLS[23] = shot(splitCell(-0.2), 134);
